Co-ordinates all aspects of pollution control, waste management, recycling, environmental health, climate change, conservation and renewable energy to ensure compliance with Environmental legislation;
Preparation of Sub-County Work Plans for all environmental activities and supervision of their implementation;
Collaborating with community and other stakeholders in environmental conservation activities;
Documenting and promoting best environmental practices;
Periodic preparation and submission of Environmental Progress Reports;
Facilitation and promotion of Citizen Participation in management of environmental affairs;
Assisting the Sub-County Administrator and liaising with other Government officers in developing strategies for better environmental service delivery;
Ensuring compliance and enforcement of Environmental Regulations within the Sub County;
Assisting the Sub-County Administrator and liaising with other county government officers in developing strategies for better environmental service delivery;
Developing and updating Sub-County Environmental Databases;
Mobilizing the public to participate in environmental conservation, landscaping and management activities within the Sub-County including liaising with NGOs;
Conducting environmental education and public awareness on environmental issues at the County/Sub-County level;
Identifying areas of Environmental concerns and ensuring they are sufficiently addressed and incorporated in Environmental management plans;
Supervising the Ward Environment officers;
Any other duties that may be assigned by the Director Environment and Natural Resources.
