Duties and Responsibilities
This is the entry and training grade for the youth polytechnic instructor’s cadre. An officer at this level will work under the guidance of a senior youth polytechnic instructor. Work will entail:-
Theoretical and practical instruction in the area of specialization;
Preparing and maintaining schemes of work, lesson notes;
Trainee records, teaching and learning materials;
Carrying out trainee’s assessment;
Ensuring proper care and maintenance of tools and equipment;
Conducting co-curricular activities, maintaining trainees ‘discipline; and
Guiding and counselling trainees.
Requirements for Appointment
For appointment to this grade, an officer must have:
Diploma or Craft Module II in any of the following disciplines Electrical and electronics, Automotive technology, Building Technology (Masonry), Hairdressing and beauty therapy, Fashion design and garment making, Metal processing technology, Information Communication Technology, AgriBusiness or any equivalent qualification from a recognized institution;
Diploma in Technical Education or Instructor training Certificate from KTTC
Experience lasting not less than two (2) years;
Certificate in computer applications from a recognized institution;Terms of Employment: Permanent & Pensionable
