Basic job summary:
The job holder will ensure the effective management of the University data processes and subjects in compliance with the Data Protection Act, No. 24 of 2019.
Duties & Responsibilities:
Act as point of contact with the office of the Data Protection Commissioner, other supervisory authorities, internal teams and other stakeholders including partners of the University;
Establish the Data Protection framework and implementation plan;
Drive implementation of essential elements of the Data Protection Act, such as; the principles of data processing, data subjects’ rights, data protection by design and by default, records of processing activities, security of processing, and notification and communication of data breaches;
Interface with data controllers and data subjects and sensitize them about their rights, obligations, and responsibilities;
Provide regular status updates to management and draw immediate attention to any compliance risks and exposure to the applicable data protection rules;
Collaborate with the Information Security function to maintain records of all data assets and exports, and maintain a data security Incident Management Plan to ensure timely remediation of incidents: including; impact assessments, security breach response, complaints, claims or notifications, and responding to subject access requests (SARs);
Identify and evaluate the University’s data processing activities;
Provide advice and instructions on how to conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs);
Monitor data management procedures and compliance within the University;
Participate in meetings with managers to ensure privacy by design at all levels;
Maintain records of processing operations;
Ensure we address all queries from data subjects within legal timeframes (e.g. delete their information from our databases);
Liaise with other organisations that process data on our behalf;
Write and update detailed guides on data protection policies;
Perform audits and determine whether we need to alter our procedures to comply with regulations;
Offer consultation on how to deal with privacy breaches;
Arrange for training on compliance for all stakeholders of the university including employees and students;
Follow up with changes in law and issue recommendations to ensure compliance.
Minimum Academic Qualifications:
Academic Qualifications
A Law degree from an accredited law school is required.
Bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in computer science or related field will be an added advantage.
Professional Certification and Training
Hold at least one Data Protection or Privacy certification.
Work Experience
Minimum of three (3) years within a compliance, legal, audit, or risk function.
Work experience in data protection and legal compliance is a plus.
Competencies and Attributes
Proficiency with software for preparing reports and presentations.
Ability to handle confidential information.
Ethical, with the ability to remain impartial and report all noncompliance.
Organizational skills with attention to detail.
Excellent communication skills.

Main Tasks:
Phone calls management
Answering phone, advising clients on their needs;
Transfer of calls to relevant staff. Front Office Management
Opening door, welcoming guests, interaction with guards respecting Embassy security guidelines;
Meeting room reservations Safaricom Management
Paperwork and activation/deactivation of Sim cards for new joiners and leavers;
Validation of invoices;
Follow up of bills and advisory on overpayment-TS to repay the office. Others
Administrative support to the Special Envoy when required
Routine correspondences to service providers and institutions including diplomatic notes, follow up on UN Commissionary and passes;
Update of contacts in contact software (Absidion) for Operations Management and Consular;
Update contact/phone lists;
Professional qualifications and experience
Diploma in either Customer care management / travels management / Communications & Public Relations or Business Administration from a reputable institution;
Front office experience, knowledge of travel arrangements and administrative support management is an asset;
Minimum 3 years’ experience in Administration / Front office / travels management;
Perfectly fluent in English language, written and spoken;
Proficiency in full Microsoft office suite;
Required skills
Highly motivated, committed and able to work in a team;
Excellent organisational skills;
Ability to communicate effectively and in a diplomatic manner at all levels;
Ability to work independently and under pressure and with minimal supervision;
High degree of adaptability/flexibility and capacity to learn;
Precise, dynamic and high level of integrity and loyalty;
Strong service and customer orientation (both internal and external).
Must be proactive, firm and respectful.

Position Summary:
Senior Investment Officer for the ADTx investment team bring deep expertise in private equity investing in emerging market, particularly in regulated financial inclusion institutions that are developing innovative digital financial services. This position should also bring operational knowledge of how financial service providers can leverage technology to scale. We expect ADTx investments in Africa will represent roughly 25-35% of total geographic allocation of the fund. The Senior Investment Officer will have influence on the ADTx strategy and portfolio allocation in the region. The candidate will collaborate with ADTx’s Operating Partner along with Accion’s Global Advisory Solutions (GLAS) team and other advisory groups to help develop digitization strategies for companies and will liaise with company boards and management teams to ensure alignment. The candidate may manage an Investment Analyst as appropriate for the size of the fund and opportunities in the region.
Position Responsibilities:
Lead the investment process along with the Managing Partners for transactions in Africa as well as support the team globally as needed; the investment process includes identifying equity investment targets consistent with the fund’s impact mission and digitization theme, leading deal execution, presenting deal analysis and investment recommendations to the Investment Committee, negotiating deals (including legal documentation), ensuring compliance with ESG policies, helping develop a digitization strategy, managing the equity investment portfolio, and developing exit alternatives;
Prepare, and oversee the preparation of detailed financial models, projections, and valuations to analyze equity investment and divestment opportunities and report to LPs;
Provide strategic support for portfolio companies, such as developing suitable alliances, raising new debt and equity, and providing input on strategic decisions, especially ESG and digitization initiatives;
Represent ADTx on portfolio company boards as appropriate;
Build co-investment consortia and develop strong relationships with co-investors;
Develop and execute along with the Managing Partners responsible commercial exit strategies for portfolio companies;
Provide ongoing support to the Operations and Finance team on portfolio company valuation and reporting;
Work closely with Managing Partners to build a strong brand and culture, while assuring that Accion Impact Management adheres to industry best practices;
Represent Accion Impact Management locally in the Africa market and globally, participating in professional development and knowledge sharing activities externally and within Accion as appropriate.
Qualifications and requirements:
10+ years of work experience of private equity focused on financial institutions, identifying investments, negotiating transactions and managing investments with deep ties and experience in Africa;
Masters level degree in business or finance;
Strong oral and written communication skills in English is required, French is a plus;
Experience implementing value creation strategies and digitally-enabled strategies with financial institutions , especially in Africa, or entrepreneurial experience a plus;
Experience in influencing board and management strategies;
Due diligence and analytical experience to identify commercially sustainable investments;
Ability to create a strong network of relationships among peers, internal partners, external constituencies and decision makers to deliver end-products;
Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, cultural sensitivity, willingness and ability to work across all levels of organization and colleagues from diverse backgrounds. Proven experience in developing senior executive presentations and communications;
Ability to work independently while working with a global team;
Willingness to embody our values of excellence, respect and passion for social change.
Excellence: Accion staff should always put forth their best effort in all activities, strive for high quality of collective and individual performance; and demonstrate honesty and integrity at all times while in the workplace and while working on behalf of the organization.
Respect: Accion staff should value one another’s roles and responsibilities as much as their own, be encouraging, and value the diverse and unique perspectives of colleagues. They should honor obligations and commitments to each other and to external partners.
Passion for Social Change: Accion staff should be committed to making a difference in the lives of those less fortunate, value the greater good of the organization over personal gain, and promote a productive workplace by acknowledging the accomplishments of others.

The Role:
The specific duties of a member appointed to the Migori County Sweet Potato Corporation (MCSPC) shall include but not limited to:
Serve as a member of the board that is committed to the advancement of the entity;
Provide technical and professional input, advice and guidance to the direction of the factory;
Participate fully in decision-making activities;
Raise the profile of Migori Sweet Potato processing in the community and at large;
Build relationships with all stakeholders.
Qualifications:
Be a Kenyan citizen;
Be a holder of at least a diploma from a recognized institution;
Have at least five (5) years experience in a sweet potato value chain;
Must have interest in sweet potato value chain;
Have demonstrated professional competence and managerial capabilities;
Demonstrate an appreciation of the diversity within the County;
Be visionary and strategic in approach;
Be a team player with an ability to network;
Demonstrate flexibility and adaptability;
Satisfy the requirements of Chapter six of the Constitution of Kenya 2010 on leadership and integrity.
How to Apply:
All interested candidates to address their applications to:THE CECM - Department of Agriculture, Livestock, Fisheries and Co-operative Development
P. O. BOX 210-40400
SUNA-MIGORI.
All applications to be hand delivered at the CECM’s Office – Department of Agriculture, Livestock, Fisheries and Co-operative Development, opposite HUDUMA Centre, to be received on or before 21st February 2023 by 5:00pm

The Policy and Legal Advisor is part of the One Humanitarian Team and will contribute to the development of our work on accountability. The post will report to the Senior Programme Manager-Accountability lead, participate in the Accountability working group and support the implementation of some of the activities as designed in the programme approach.
The role will contribute to provide legal advice and develop policy positions and discussion papers on issues related to our accountability work, ensuring that the organisation contributes to the strategic debates in the sector and positions itself to remain fit for purpose.
EXPERIENCE AND SKILLS
Excellent knowledge of International Criminal Law, International Human Rights and International Humanitarian Law and issues related to accountability and fight against impunity. Strong knowledge of children’s rights is desirable;
Excellent knowledge of the institutional and legal framework governing international judicial and non-judicial accountability mechanisms;
Strong analytical skills, and an ability to distil large amounts of information and communicate it effectively;
Minimum 5 years of related experience, including in the NGO sector;
Track record of developing and influencing policy;
Significant ability to produce high-quality policy documents (briefs, key messages, guides, etc.) with short deadlines;
Attention to detail and ability to follow tasks and ideas through to completion;
Strong analytical and creative problem-solving skills to tackle complex problems;
Able to operate effectively and flexibly within an evolving portfolio of work;
Excellent interpersonal skills, able to communicate with colleagues in a dispersed, creative and multicultural professional environment;
Strong organisation skills, with a proven ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines;
Self-motivated and able to take initiative, working with limited supervision
Ability to maintain high attention to detail in pressurised environments.
Ability to work on own initiative with a ‘can do' attitude.
Fluency in English; other languages desirable
Commitment to the values and principles of Save the Children

Contracts Management
Manage a portfolio of contracts from multiple donors including the United States Government, Foreign Governments and Private Foundations
Review and negotiate terms and conditions with donors, clients, vendors and other suppliers. Create complex modifications to subcontracts
Advise and train employees on contract and compliance topics, policies and procedures
Ensure compliance with contract/subcontract requirements
Advise on and/or help prepare cost and pricing proposals in coordination with technical staff and design lab
Administer, manage and monitor subcontracts/subawards including issuing RFPs/RFAs, reviewing proposals, negotiating budget, determining appropriate contracting mechanism, draft/amend subcontracts, obtain necessary approvals, monitor compliance and complete closeout
Lead contract budget realignments with donors
Prepare RFQs, review quotes and assist in selecting vendor, prepare justifications
Provide general contract implementation support to all offices
Negotiate and manage consulting agreements
Provide additional support as required in area of expertise
Requirements
BA/BS and 5+ years experience or graduate degree and 3+ years experience;
Work experience in international development procurement and contracts/subcontracts management;
Experience with USG rules, regulations and FAR/OMB. USAID, CDC, private foundation and corporation contracts experience;
Experience preparing complex budgets in Excel for multi-year cost proposal submissions preferred;
Adept at communicating technical information to non-technical audiences;
A team player, motivated to provide subject matter expertise with a collaborative, customer service orientation;
Demonstrated ability to complete tasks quickly, thoroughly and conscientiously with attention to detail and a responsive, ‘can-do’ attitude;
A thoughtful systems thinker with grounded, pragmatic understanding of the complexities of our work;
Demonstrated ability to engage effectively with external vendors and stakeholders;
Full English fluency, second language a plus;
Outstanding cross-cultural communication skills, including the ability to relate respectfully with staff at all levels, ages, genders, nationalities and orientations as well as across work areas.

Specific Duties Will Include
The GCI secretariat is looking for a consultant to lead the research, drafting, development and finalization of a study on green customs and gender.
Preparing a research plan, methodology and outline/structure for the envisaged publication, including information about the data collection tools and the analytical approach;
Conducting a comprehensive desk review of primary resources and related bibliography in relation to gender and customs;
Preparing a questionnaire for the collection of gender-related qualitative and quantitative data relating to the GCI covered agreements and the gender dimensions of the trade of environmental commodities regulated under those agreements; the gender policies and procedures of the GCI partners; and gender aspects of selected customs and border control administration and identify target groups for the dissemination of the questionnaires;
Carrying out interviews, as needed, with relevant stakeholders such as government officials, customs and border enforcement institutes and officers, the World Customs Organization, GCI partners, civil society organization, community groups and women organizations;
Analyzing collected data, drafting the study and incorporating feedback received from UNEP and relevant stakeholders;
Presenting the publication’s findings and recommendations in awareness raising and capacity-building events as well as in communication products.
Qualifications/special Skills
Advanced university degree in social sciences, environmental studies, gender studies, sustainable development or related fields.
Familiarity with gender issues in general and practical experience in collection of gender-disaggregated data;
At least seven years of experience in gender analysis, gender discrimination or equality, preferably within the context of environmental protection or sustainable development.
Special Knowledge & Skills
Knowledge of the UN system
Certification in data analytics, business analytics or data science programmes.
A combination of excellent problem solving communication and interpersonal skills.
Ability to work in a fast-paced, multitasking environment.
